MatchedObjectDescriptor.QualificationSummary:
GS-11: In addition to the Basic Requirements for this position, your resume must also demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the GS-09 grade level or pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate the following:
Experience investigating personnel exposure mishaps, spills, and hazardous conditions/incidents;
Extensive experience reviewing plans, designs, technical work documents/specifications for work processes, operations, facilities, buildings and ships to identify health hazards and proper controls;
Experience managing occupational exposure control programs for chemical, physical, and biological stressor in the workplace;
Experience developing, reviewing, auditing, coordinating and/or providing occupational health training and education;
Experience developing formal guidance as necessary to ensure activity compliance. GS-09: In addition to the Basic Requirements for this position, your resume must also demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the GS-07 grade level or pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate the following:
Experience analyzing exposure sampling data to identify exposure trends;
Extensive experience investigating personnel exposure mishaps, spills, and hazardous conditions/incidents;
Experience reviewing and implementing national, federal, defense, and Navy occupational health standards, manuals, reports and other formal written communication;
Experience conducting surveys and evaluation reports to recommend corrective action. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management website:
https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=List-by-Occupational-Series Experience refers to paid and unpaid experience, including volunteer work done through National Service programs (e.g., professional, philanthropic, religious, spiritual, community, student, social). Volunteer work helps build critical competencies, knowledge, and skills and can provide valuable training and experience that translates directly to paid employment.
